	__stage_0__NoteShape__00000015_.Name = `PIT Report-Many thruster pulses are less  FDIR in the  The FMCs see chamber pressure over a data bus from the  but the chamber pressure is only sent to the ground with a sample rate for recording every  limiting insight into thruster performance. This does not meet Nyquist Criterion for capturing the chamber pressure signal. As a result, aliasing effects may occur for pulses shorter than  where high-frequency components of the pressure signal are misrepresented or lost, further complicating accurate reconstruction of thruster behavior.  `
