	__stage_0__NoteShape__00000019_.Name = `PIT Report-B1.3.3.1.1.1 Heat identifies that excessive heating could cause the poppet to extrude, reducing flow. Poppet extrusion was observed in the post-test tear down of the WSTF (White Sands Test Facility) thruster unit.

The initial heating was caused by the internal doghouse temperatures (addressed in C4.1 Thermal) and the follow-on heating induced by B1.3.3.1.4.2 RCS Thermal Soakback. This caused excessive temperatures beyond the capability of the thruster softgoods, causing the Teflon poppet to extrude. The evidence supports this being a contributor to the thruster fail-offs.`
	__stage_0__NoteShape__00000019_.IsLayoutDirectionDifferent = false
	__stage_0__NoteShape__00000019_.X = 1325.045052
	__stage_0__NoteShape__00000019_.Y = 1477.461652
